(:adr
  :id "ADR-0061"
  :shortcode "D61"
  :title "Agent Goal Perception, Semantic Validation Primitives, and Epistemic Infrastructure Readiness"
  :status :active
  :date "2026-09-10"
  :cluster "ai-architecture/cognition"
  :deciders ["architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "Attention-based language models lack intrinsic deliberation loops and often mistake linguistic fluency for goal comprehension. Without rigid mathematical and operational grounding, agents exhibit goal drift across multi-turn trajectories, premature victory claims (hallucinatory settlement), and superficial satisfaction of prompt requests without fulfilling underlying architectural invariants. To ensure sovereign reliability, a rigorous foundation must define how agents perceive, operationalize, and physically validate goals, and benchmark whether the system infrastructure is fully equipped to enforce these guarantees."
  :drivers [
    "Epistemic Operationalization: Define goal comprehension strictly as the ability to construct a falsifiable verification gate before mutating state"
    "Deliberation Gap Elimination: Overcome feed-forward attention limits via structured intent schemas (:Intent, :Capabilities, :Directives, :Context, :Invariants)"
    "Physical Receipt Verification: Forbid speculative self-grading by requiring immutable execution evidence with non-vacuous assertion counts"
    "Multi-Lens Triangulation: Validate all complex goals across theoretical bounds, runtime telemetry, and adversarial falsification"
    "Typestate Isolation: Prevent cognitive goal degradation by bounding operational scopes to cohesive 120-280 line state machines"
  ]
  :decision "Adopt ADR-0061 (D61) establishing the normative standard for Agent Goal Perception and Validation across the AgentScript ecosystem. Codify the 4-level Goal Hierarchy (Linguistic Intent, Structured Intent, Operational Task DAG, and Homeostatic Verification Gate). Declare the monorepo infrastructure fully ready under the 7-tier verification gate (asl gate), the 5-dimension consistency engine (asl audit consistency), and physical execution receipts (receipts.asn). Deploy the discrete Semantic Goal Validator in codebase intelligence to detect and prevent intent drift before state mutation."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D56" "D57" "D58" "D59" "D60" "D61"]
  :tasks [
    "T416MetaResearch"
    "T416DesignSystem"
    "T416AlgoSearch"
    "T416Coordination"
    "T416SelfCorrect"
    "T416Settle"
  ]
  :outcomes [
    "Formalized the mathematical and cognitive mechanics of agent goal perception and validation"
    "Benchmarked full monorepo infrastructure readiness across all 7 verification tiers"
    "Identified empirical research gaps in runtime intent divergence and automated triangulation"
    "Codified discrete epistemic primitives preventing ungrounded speculation"
  ]
  :consequences [
    (:pos "Eliminates premature settlement and hallucinatory victory declarations monorepo-wide")
    (:pos "Grounds every goal in a machine-executable, falsifiable verification predicate")
    (:pos "Provides transparent infrastructure readiness criteria for all external agent IDE integrations")
    (:neg "Requires all work items to declare explicit falsifiable gates and non-vacuous assertions")
  ])
